---
title: Grilled Chicken Thighs and Corn with Lime-Basil Butter
description: Lime and garlic chicken thighs grilled next to sweet corn, with a basil butter that melts over both.
tags: [grill, midsummer]
course: main
icons: [drumstick, corn, butter]
source:
  name: NYT Cooking
  author: Clare de Boer
  url: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1025669-grilled-chicken-thighs-and-corn-with-lime-basil-butter
servings: 4
prep time: 10m
cook time: 30m
---

= Chicken

Zest the @limes{2} and save the zest for the butter. Put the @boneless, skinless chicken thighs{2%lb} in a #large bowl{} with the @garlic cloves{3}(finely grated), @olive oil{1%tbsp}, @kosher salt{1 3/4%tsp} and the juice of 1 lime. Toss to coat. Leave it at room temperature while the grill heats.

> **Marinating ahead** — Better still, cover the bowl and refrigerate it overnight.

= Lime-Basil Butter

Put the @unsalted butter{57%g}(4 tbsp, at room temperature), the lime zest, @basil leaves{3/4%cup}, @&kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and @black pepper{1%tsp}(freshly ground, plus more to finish) in a #food processor{}. Run it until the basil is chopped and worked into the butter.

> **Making ahead** — The butter keeps in the fridge overnight. Take it out with the chicken and set it near the grill to soften.

= Grilling

Light the #grill{} to medium-high. Put the @ears of corn{4}(shucked) on one side and turn them every 3 minutes or so, until cooked through and lightly charred, ~corn{10-20%minutes} in all.

Take the corn off the grill and slice off the charred kernels. Pile them on a #serving platter{} and top with some of the basil butter.

While the corn cooks, lay the chicken on the grill, flat sides down. Leave it until it lets go of the grates easily, ~char{5-7%minutes}. Turn each piece slightly without flipping it, so the first side picks up more color.

When parts of the first side are chestnut brown, flip the chicken and grill for another ~grill{3-5%minutes}. Keep turning and flipping every few minutes until it's cooked through.

> **Checking the chicken** — Poke a knife into the thickest part. The juices should run clear, with no translucent meat.

Slice each thigh in half across its widest part and set the slices on the corn. Spoon the rest of the basil butter over the hot chicken. Scatter the remaining @&basil leaves{1/4%cup} on top and squeeze over the second lime. Finish with @flaky sea salt{} and more black pepper. Don't skip the lime or the salt.
